/**
 * notes-data.js — B.Tech. (Biotechnology) course catalogue + Google Drive resources
 * Source: ICAR Sixth Deans' Committee Report, Vol. 1 — "Semester-Wise Course Distribution"
 *         (PDF pages 4–6, printed pages 577–579) and credit-hour summary tables.
 *
 * HOW TO ADD A GOOGLE DRIVE LINK
 * ------------------------------
 * 1. Find the course in NOTES_COURSES below (search by its title).
 * 2. Put the resource(s) inside its `resources: [ ... ]` array, e.g.
 *
 *      resources: [
 *        { id: 'cell-bio-complete', title: 'Complete Lecture Notes', type: 'notes',
 *          format: 'PDF', description: 'Units 1–5',
 *          driveUrl: 'https://drive.google.com/file/d/XXXXXXXX/view?usp=sharing' }
 *      ]
 *
 *    - `driveUrl` is used exactly as written (never rewritten). Leave it '' to keep a
 *      placeholder that shows as "coming soon" (the course then counts as "partially available"
 *      if other resources are configured).
 *    - `type` is one of: notes | unit | lecture | practical | pyq | revision | other
 *    - Remove a link: delete the resource object (or set driveUrl: '').
 * 3. In Drive, set the file to "Anyone with the link → Viewer" so students are not asked for access.
 *
 * Only drive.google.com / docs.google.com / drive.usercontent.google.com https links are accepted.
 * No course codes are published in the source document, so none are included.
 */
